<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss bond market closing report.</title>
<headline>Swiss bond market closing report.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss bonds ended firmer while the short end lagged, with EuroSwiss futures finishing slightly lower. Overall trade was very quiet, lacking new fundamentals. Ten-year cash yields edge down towards 3.50 pct.</p>
<p>-- Tuesday's closing prices as follows:</p>
<p>Conf futures  CONFc1 ends up 10 at 120.04.</p>
<p>Comi medium-term bond  COMIc1 up three at 111.52</p>
<p>Euro Swiss francs  FESc1 down one at 98.16</p>
<p>4-1/2 Jun 2007 bond  0#CH470458= 108.10/20 yld 3.52 pct</p>
<p>(Close Monday 108.02/12 yield 3.529 pct</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
